  "chapter": 785,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 140 Chapter 785\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4716-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the State Technology Law, in relation to requiring\n        the Office of Information Technology Services to cooperate  with\n        all State agencies in the implementation of language translation\n        technology\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill requires the Office of Information Technology Services (ITS)\nto assist State agencies in implementing language translation technology\non  their  websites  within 30 days for all sites containing information\nabout COVID-19, or programs, benefits or services related  to  COVID-19.\nThe  language  translation  technology must allow users to translate the\ntext of the website into, at least, the twelve most  common  non-English\nlanguages  spoken by individuals with limited-English proficiency in the\nState of New York. All other State agency websites would be required  to\nincorporate such technology within 90 days.\n \n  To ensure this bill can be successfully implemented, I have secured an\nagreement  with  the Legislature to extend the implementation dates from\n30 days to 60 days for all COVID-19 related websites, and 90 days  to  6\nmonths of all other websites.\n \n  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
